## 12. Points for the AUDIT

Neutral points for the A08 AUDIT, each citing the statements it rests on. "Boundary" marks a point whose code or record another topic or part owns; it is reported, not resolved. No verdict is given; nothing is classified.

- P03-AP01 — Indirect effects of the observer on the order path: the texts say the observer "NEVER blocks/delays placement and NEVER raises into the pipeline", which holds for the call and the observer's own code (reached after placement; non-waiting hand-off; nothing written that the order path reads); its worker shares with the order path the live broker client and the process's rate limiter, the database's single write lock (one `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` insert with a `synchronous = FULL` commit per row) and interpreter time, and no text states an intent or a bound for these (P03-S101 to P03-S111, P03-S193). Boundary: A01 and A04 for the client and the limiter (A01 C38a, B-11, A04 RL-05, RL-11; part P02 primary), A03 for the store's locking.
- P03-AP02 — As of when the V1 evidence is computed (A05 HA-04's A08 side): the stated question is whether buying into resistance can be detected "before the outcome is known", but each analysis fetches windows that end when the worker reaches the candidate, after any queue wait and with cached lists up to 1800 s old, and nothing truncates the candles to the placement-time stamp or drops a still-forming last candle; a row can therefore rest partly on price action after the entry (P03-S043, P03-S053, P03-S057, P03-S168, P03-S194). Whether the broker returned forming candles is UNKNOWN (P03-U03).
- P03-AP03 — What the breakout flags measure: the "breakout candle" is the last element of the 30-minute list at processing time, not a candle tied to the entry; the "broken" zone is the nearest lower resistance (or upper support) at any distance and of any confidence; a "breakout" is counted whenever the last close is beyond that zone's edge, without any candle having crossed it; `NO_VOLUME_CONFIRMATION` is not possible when the average volume is 0 and compares a possibly partial last candle's volume with full candles (P03-S052, P03-S053, P03-S070 to P03-S072, P03-S184). Against the docstring's "breakout candle lacks follow-through" and "breakout without a volume surge" (P03-S014).
- P03-AP04 — The flag table and the committed comment against the code: `BUYING_INTO_RESISTANCE` and its mirror test only the nearest zone with a one-sided pad; `LOW_CONFIDENCE_STRUCTURE` requires the entry to be "into" the nearest zone; `WEAK_BREAKOUT` includes a poke-and-fail; `NO_CLEAR_STRUCTURE` is raised only when no zone exists at all, a LOW zone counting as structure, and is also the only flag of a `FETCH_FAILED` row; the comment "entry within this % of a HIGH zone" (`config/system_config.yaml` L517) describes a pad the code applies to the nearest zone of any confidence; `PATHS.md` L418 omits `SELLING_INTO_SUPPORT` (P03-S014, P03-S044, P03-S048, P03-S066 to P03-S069, P03-S080, P03-S196, P03-S203).
- P03-AP05 — Placed candidates that leave no row: the schema calls the table "One row per PLACED candidate" (`core/schema.sql` L1248), but a candidate leaves no row when the queue is full (one WARNING), when it is still queued at `stop` (no log line), when the analysis raises (one ERROR) or when the insert fails, a NULL `created_at` after a clock failure included (one ERROR); nothing in the table records these gaps (P03-S033, P03-S038, P03-S055, P03-S086, P03-S092).
- P03-AP06 — "A later run picks it up" (A03 U-25's A08 side; A07 XS-12): every run selects only its date's rows and the declared 15:58 run passes no date, so a row skipped as open is revisited only by a run given that date (P03-S115, P03-S124, P03-S135, P03-S167). The finding is A03's U-25; this point adds the guard's effect on manual runs (P03-AP07).
- P03-AP07 — The guard and manual runs: `_cron_main`'s docstring and the commit message of `09ea7254cc47b5c211fb6d408d92d3e62d859b73` say the guard is outside `main()` "so a manual/ad-hoc run on a non-trading day is never blocked", but the script's only command-line entry calls `_cron_main()`, so a documented manual run on a weekend or NSE holiday, a re-run for an earlier date included, is skipped with exit status 0 and can write a SKIPPED heartbeat; only a call of `main()` from Python code bypasses it (P03-S127, P03-S130, P03-S131, P03-S213). Boundary: A16 for the guard and for the same entry pattern in the other scripts of that commit.
- P03-AP08 — Dates and time zones in the backfill: rows are selected by SQLite's `date(ts)`, the UTC date of the offset IST stamps (the IST date only from 05:30 IST); the default date falls back to the host's local date when `now_ist` fails; the guard's "today" is the IST date; the schedule runs in the host's cron time zone, which the cron file's comment says is IST but does not set (P03-S116, P03-S125, P03-S128, P03-S134, P03-S207). Boundary: A03 (H-11, the `DATE()` reading), A16 (the cron time zone).
- P03-AP09 — The backfill and the V2 divert's rows (latent at the committed values, the V2 path being off): the selection does not filter on `detector_version`, so `snr-v2` divert rows are backfilled too; a divert row whose signal was never placed is closed as `NO_TRADE` on the comment's premise "Observer fires post-placement", which a pre-placement row does not meet; a signal placed through the retest path can have a divert row and an observer row, and the A15 report keeps the one with the earlier `created_at` text, the two rows having different time forms (P03-S093, P03-S094, P03-S096, P03-S115, P03-S122). Boundary: part P04 (the divert row), A15 (the report), A03 (H-11).
- P03-AP10 — Two stop buffers for one formula (A02 K-22's A08 side; primary part P04): the V1 proposal's stop uses `retest_sl_buffer_pct`, a loader field absent from the committed file (0.3), while the V2 stop uses the committed `sl_buffer_pct` (0.2), with the same `band_low × (1 − pct/100)` formula (P03-S060, P03-S075, P03-S077, P03-S178).
- P03-AP11 — The outcome values written by the backfill: `NO_FILL` is written for cancelled, failed and rejected trades together with whatever fill price and P&L the trade row holds; a closed trade without P&L gets `UNKNOWN`; `actual_result` falls back to the status when `exit_reason` is empty; none of these value sets is stated in a column comment or a document read for this part (P03-S118, P03-S121). Boundary: A10 and A03 for what a cancelled, failed or rejected trade row can hold.
- P03-AP12 — The store's comment on the insert columns (A03's file; boundary): "actual_*/win_loss/pnl/hypothetical_retest_result are EOD-backfilled and intentionally absent here" (`core/state_store.py` L1967 to L1969), while `actual_fill` is in `_SR_INSERT_COLS` (L1972) and both A08 writers pass it as `None` (P03-S081, P03-S088, P03-S196).
- P03-AP13 — The telemetry registry's line references (A02's file, A15's mechanism; boundary): `config/expected_managers.yaml` L118 to L123 cite `main.py:2979`, `yaml:407` and `detector.py:254 _write`, which match none of the baseline's lines (`main.py` L3494, `config/system_config.yaml` L509, `sr_detector/detector.py` L259 and L298) (P03-S098, P03-S099).
- P03-AP14 — The legacy documents' account of the observer: `PATHS.md` and `docs/SYSTEM_MAP.md` describe the seam as two call sites ("BOTH `_process_one` + `continue_from_gate`"; "both paths"), while the baseline has three, the first in `_admit_and_place`; `PATHS.md` L417 gives the flag as `enabled: false`, the committed value being `true`; the arming commit calls the observer "read-only", while it writes its rows; the A08 inventory's section 2.1 lists only L1550 (P03-S101, P03-S203, P03-S204, P03-S214; noted for revision in `<workspace>/status/AGENTS_REGISTER_STUDY.md`).
- P03-AP15 — The nearest zones and distances in the row: the recorded "nearest resistance" can lie below the entry (and the "nearest support" above it) when no zone is on the expected side, its distance is then negative, distances are measured to the zone's centre, and the column comments state no unit or sign; the A15 report displays these columns (P03-S064, P03-S065, P03-S091, P03-S096).
- P03-AP16 — Minor contract points: the JSON columns can hold the non-standard tokens `NaN` and `Infinity` and are spaced differently by the two writers (P03-S084); `stop` reports neither a timed-out join nor the candidates it leaves in the queue, and a `start` after a timed-out `stop` would run a second worker (no caller does so) (P03-S033); `_cfg` is stored and never read, and the detector's `_mode` serves only a log line (P03-S024).

